  "_comment": "This manifest is the single authoritative source for course-level config (playback mode, translations, transliteration, which packages exist, and — as of this update — each package's own display label). The app should always read that config from here, never by inspecting an individual package JSON's own top-level fields, or by guessing a label from position — even though French/Spanish package files also happen to carry course_id/playback/translations themselves for human-readability and standalone validity, the running app must not branch on those. One source of truth avoids the desync class of bug we hit earlier in this project (the IS_ADMIN duplication). Chinese100_0N.json files carry none of these fields at all and are untouched — this manifest supplies their course-level config entirely from here. NOTE: Chinese's own code path (TL_PACK_LABELS in index.html) does NOT read the 'label' field below — it's included here for data consistency and any future migration, but Chinese's existing, working label system is intentionally left untouched. Only the generic (TTS) course system actually reads 'label' from here.",
